# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the committed
# record of what the app needs to run.
#
# One file, read by three things: `docker compose` (from this directory) decides
# what the container is called, the Prisma CLI loads it by an explicit path in
# `packages/db/prisma7.config.ts`, and `apps/web/next.config.ts` does the same —
# because Next reads environment files from the app directory, and a second copy
# under `apps/web` is a second thing to forget to change.

# What the app connects with. With `docker compose up -d` this must match the
# POSTGRES_* values below.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/my_ecommerce?schema=public"

# Only needed by Prisma's own local server. `migrate dev` replays the migration
# history into a second, empty database to detect drift; a real Postgres creates
# that shadow database on demand, and the local one hands you a URL instead —
# `prisma dev ls` prints it. Leave this out when using docker compose.
# SHADOW_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:51215/template1?sslmode=disable"

# Content translation (optional).
#
# With a key set, saving a product, category, blog post or blog category in the
# admin also writes its German, French, Portuguese and Spanish translations;
# without one, content simply stays English and the admin says so. Nothing else
# depends on it, so a checkout without either key runs exactly as it did before.
#
# Two engines are wired, and the key that is present decides which runs —
# DeepSeek when both are set, since it is the better of the two at this copy.
# `apps/web/lib/i18n/translate/engine.ts` holds that rule; both keys are read
# server-side only.
#
# DeepSeek is a language model: it is told the shop's voice and the register to
# write in, so product copy comes back in the tone the hand-written catalogs
# use, and markdown survives. It costs a fraction of a cent per product.
# Register at platform.deepseek.com — the key goes here, and the model id is a
# setting because DeepSeek retires them (`deepseek-chat` was retired in July
# 2026; `deepseek-flash` is current).
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=""
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL="deepseek-flash"

# DeepL is a translation service: faster, cheaper per character, and it never
# invents a sentence — but it follows instructions about tone less well. Its
# API Free plan covers 500,000 characters a month (roughly 300 products) and
# needs no card at deepl.com/pro-api, the "API Free" column. A free key ends in
# `:fx`, which is how the client knows to call the free host.
# DEEPL_API_KEY=""

# What the container is created with.
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_DB=my_ecommerce

# Change this if something else already listens on 5432.
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
